abstract: >-
  Analysis code, frozen held-out predictions, fitted model artifacts, and
  reference outputs for a retrospective secondary analysis of five publicly
  available clinical prediction datasets, examining within-dataset subgroup
  sensitivity differences across sex, age, and race/ethnicity, and how
  prevalence standardization and operating thresholds affect their
  interpretation. All data-derived preprocessing is fitted inside each
  cross-validation and calibration fold on that fold's training observations
  only. The Diabetes-130 dataset is partitioned, cross-validated, calibrated,
  and resampled at the patient level, with uncertainty from a joint
  patient-cluster bootstrap.
keywords:
  - clinical prediction models
  - machine learning
  - algorithmic bias
  - health equity
  - model evaluation
  - model calibration
